# Every route is client-side (vue-router, history mode), so any path Cloudflare
# doesn't recognize as a real file has to resolve to the shell. This is the
# Cloudflare Pages equivalent of vercel.json's catch-all rewrite — without it,
# a hard reload on e.g. /today 404s because there is no file at that path.
#
# The trailing `!` (force) is required, not decorative: Cloudflare Pages
# normalizes `/index.html` down to `/` as a built-in step, and without the
# force flag its loop-detector sees `/ -> /index.html -> (normalized) / -> ...`
# and rejects the whole file at deploy time with "Infinite loop detected".
# `!` tells it to serve this rule as-is and skip that normalization pass.
/*  /index.html  200!
